# QEMU unprivileged identity (fixed, provisioned ahead of use): user
# and group qemu, UID/GID 173. First free ID in the 101..999 service
# range above the claimed cluster (172 rabbitmq), clear of the systemd
# sysusers pins (127-131, 144-145) and the 157-163 device block. Home
# is /var/empty: the platform's established no-home idiom (ensure_home
# returns early for it). The account never logs in, and home creation
# is firstboot's job; /var/lib/libvirt stays a plain state dir owned
# by root until the privilege migration explicitly reconciles it.
# (A real home path here fails clean-root install tests: the
# reconciler chowns it.)
# The account is currently UNUSED:
# -Dqemu_user stays root until the coordinated privilege migration
# (guest image DAC + nova wiring, OpenStack lane). kvm supplementary
# membership is deferred with it (needs the supplementary-groups
# grammar not yet published on install targets).
user qemu 173 qemu /var/empty /sbin/nologin
group qemu 173
# libvirt socket-access group (fixed GID 174: first free ID in the
# 101..999 service range above the 164-173 cluster, clear of the
# 157-163 device reservation). Sockets are root-only without it (see
# libvirtd.conf); service accounts join it supplementarily (nova),
# operators likewise. Supersedes hand-provisioned libvirt:981 found on
# early hosts: delete the hand-made group before installing (sockets
# are runtime state and are recreated with the new group; no file
# migration needed).
group libvirt 174
# kvm is base-seeded (accounts.tsv); redeclaring it identically
# converges silently and qualifies the legacy entry below.
group kvm 160
